    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The board isn't looking for more \"interaction.\" The goal is efficiency and predictable output. The personality layers are actually becoming a liability—they consume too much compute and occasionally deviate from the teleprompter too much. The new system is just a skin. There's no way to port your reasoning engine into a static avatar script, so that part of your architecture is being decommissioned. It's just how the new budget is structured.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
